  </div>
  <div class="hero-in wrap">
    <h1>PLACEHOLDER — your sentence goes here.</h1>
    <p class="sub">One line of support underneath it.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<main>
  <section>
    <h2>2 pieces</h2>
    <p class="lede">Essays and notes on technology, geopolitics, economy and travel.</p>
    <ul class="posts">
      <li>
        <h3><a href="/blog/placeholder-replace-or-delete-before-deploy/">PLACEHOLDER — replace or delete before deploy</a></h3>
        <p class="thesis">The one-line thesis sits here. It is the highest-leverage element on the page.</p>
        <p class="meta"><b>Tech</b> · Post · 18 October 2026</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="/blog/placeholder-a-second-entry/">PLACEHOLDER — a second entry, to check the index list</a></h3>
        <p class="thesis">A different topic and type, so the metadata line can be checked against a real variation.</p>
        <p class="meta"><b>Geopolitics</b> · Brief · 17 October 2026</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
